text "This would make software that relies on these semantics fail: for example, a speech browser that allowed a blind user to navigate tables in the document would report the quote above as a table, confusing the user; similarly, a tool that extracted titles of works from pages would extract \"Ernest\" as the title of a work, even though it's actually a person's name, not a title."
