h3 3.2.5.3 Transparent content models
text "Some elements are described as ; they have \"transparent\" in the description of their content model. The content model of a  element is derived from the content model of its parent element: the elements required in the part of the content model that is \"transparent\" are the same elements as required in the part of the content model of the parent of the transparent element in which the transparent element finds itself."
row
