text Let  be a view of the DOM that replaces all , , , and  elements in the document with their . Then, in , for each run of sibling  nodes uninterrupted by other types of content, in an element that accepts content other than  as well as , let  be the first node of the run, and let  be the last node of the run. For each such run that consists of at least one node that is neither  nor , a paragraph exists in the original DOM from immediately before  to immediately after . (Paragraphs can thus span across , , , and  elements.)
